<%#
# The list of models of one setting

A plain `<select>` (it works without a script and is what the form posts); a script turns it into a searchable list with
the price and the badges of every model. The first option is «Встроенная» (an empty value: the platform decides). The
value that is saved always stays selected, even when the list does not offer it any more: it is marked and never replaced
by the first option.

## Local variables:

- `slot`: a `SuperAdmin::AiModelsPage::Slot` of a model setting (`choices` is set).
- `placeholder` (optional): the text of the empty option of a list that has no built-in model (the list to add a model to the short list).
%>
<%
  choices = slot.choices
  shown = slot.input.to_s.strip
  stored = slot.value.to_s.strip
  known = choices.include?(shown) || shown.blank?
%>
<select name="app_config[<%= slot.key %>]" id="app_config_<%= slot.key %>" data-model-select data-stored="<%= stored %>" data-builtin-id="<%= choices.builtin_id %>"
        <%= 'aria-invalid="true"'.html_safe if slot.invalid? %>>
  <%= ai_builtin_option(choices, shown) %>
  <% if choices.missing %>
    <optgroup label="<%= t('super_admin.app_config.captain.models.saved_group') %>">
      <%= ai_model_option(choices.missing, shown) %>
    </optgroup>
  <% end %>
  <% unless known || shown == choices.missing&.id %>
    <%# what was sent and refused: it stays selected so that the admin sees what he entered %>
    <optgroup label="<%= t('super_admin.app_config.captain.models.saved_group') %>">
      <%= ai_model_option(@ai_models_page.options.describe(shown, key: slot.key), shown) %>
    </optgroup>
  <% end %>
  <% choices.groups.each do |title, options| %>
    <optgroup label="<%= title %>">
      <% options.each do |option| %>
        <%= ai_model_option(option, shown) %>
      <% end %>
    </optgroup>
  <% end %>
</select>
